{"title":"Career Roadmap · Research Assistant","role":"Research Assistant","summary":"A Research Assistant in Microbiology supports scientific investigations involving microorganisms, infectious agents, host–microbe interactions, biotechnology, antimicrobial research, environmental microbiology, and related biological systems.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Microbiology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Research Assistant in Microbiology supports scientific investigations involving microorganisms, infectious agents, host–microbe interactions, biotechnology, antimicrobial research, environmental microbiology, and related biological systems."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Experimental design support"},{"text":"Microbial culture"},{"text":"Sample preparation"},{"text":"Microscopy"},{"text":"Molecular biology assays"},{"text":"PCR-based analysis"},{"text":"Data collection"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Laboratory documentation"},{"text":"Research reporting"},{"text":"Maintaining cultures and laboratory records"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc Microbiology student, the strongest pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Microbiology","Research Internship/Project","M.Sc Microbiology/Biotechnology","Research Assistant","Research Scientist","Specialized Researcher"]},{"type":"p","text":"A postgraduate degree is generally valuable for progressing from laboratory support roles into independent research positions."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc Microbiology, laboratory skills, molecular biology, research projects"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"M.Sc Microbiology/Biotechnology + Research Assistant/Pr